<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  The reference's schema of the clinic InfoCube ZCLVISIT (docs/clinic-demo.md), the reference scenario for BW
  hierarchies (docs/next-steps.md, Reference scenario), as the test catalog and cube ZCLHIER (the demo's own catalog
  ZCLVISIT is SAP's, and a cube name is one cube of the server). It is SAP's accepted schema of the catalog ZCLVISIT
  (the schema generator's proposal) without its annotations (olap4abap's extensions, which the reference does not
  know) and with the dimension tables named by their placeholders (ZZXXMLA1_C_<characteristic>, as in FoodmartBW.xml),
  plus the BW hierarchy ZCLDIAG_ICD of the diagnosis as a balanced level hierarchy, Level 01 to Level 04, a member on
  the level of its depth as olap4abap serves it (docs/next-steps.md, Reference scenario, decided 2026-10-16). SAP
  serves ClinicBW-sap.xml as ZCLHIER: the same schema with the hierarchy in olap4abap's form; the test compares the
  answers of the catalogs of the same name.

  The reference database (scripts/build-bw-reference-db.py) holds BW's tables of the cube, the characteristics' views
  and, computed from the copy of the hierarchy (ZZXXMLA1_CL_BW_HIERARCHY_COPY) at the version current at the export,
  its flattened table ZZXXMLA1_HL_ZCLDIAG_ICD: a row per value SID (the fact's SID_ZCLDIAG joins it), per level its
  member's key Lnn_SID (the node's SID: negative for a text node, the value's SID for a value), name Lnn_NAME (a text
  node's technical name or a value's key, # for the initial value, as BW's MDX names them) and Lnn_POS (its position
  among its siblings, BW's order). Every value is a leaf (the initial one under NOT_RECORDED > NO_DIAGNOSIS) and BW
  suppresses the not-assigned node, so the hierarchy has no REST_H.

  The dimension ZCLDIAG has no table of its own: the reference gives every hierarchy of a dimension with a table that
  table (RolapHierarchy), so each hierarchy names its own; the flat one is first, so the drill-through's attributes
  (sourceAttribute) bind to the characteristic's view.
-->
